                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Neon Struct - review\n\nThis was a good lite-immersive sim. Many features from some other imsims aren't here but that is actually not a bad thing, at least in my opinion. For example, you do not carry any guns but you can use a takedown to dispose of enemies and while at first it feels constrained to not have lethal options available, it doesn't hurt the gameplay. Fighting isn't the main point here, but you do have some gadgets that are useful in most places. It isn't a very long one but there is no filler here and the plot manages to keep progressing interesting. Overall it is a nice game for any imsim fans.\n\nGraphical style is good and atmospheric. Musical side of things are ok as well.\nAfter finishing the game, I was left feeling that I'd wish for Neon Struct 2. Add levels, items, enemies and some features and it would be a great sequel. This game is very copacetic but a sequel could reach new heights.",
